      "text": "オオバイヌビワ は、クワ科イチジク属の樹木の一つ。大きな幅広い葉をつける。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Ficus septica」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ficus_septica",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1373620130,
      "text": "Ficus septica, also known as the Hauili fig tree, is a species of shrub or tree in the family Moraceae. It is native to Malesia, Taiwan, the Ryukyu Islands, Papuasia, Queensland in northern Australia, the Santa Cruz Islands, and Vanuatu.\nIt grows in lowland tropical moist forests, often at forest edges and in degraded environments. The seeds of this species are dispersed by numerous species, including fruit bats (Megachiroptera) when present."
    }
